  "body": "Follow-up to #1278 / PR #1287.\n\nWhat happens: since #1278, `camcraft-ui.exe` is a GUI-subsystem exe. Launched from a terminal it attaches to that console (std handles pointed at `CONOUT$`), and a redirect (`> log.txt 2>&1`) or pipe keeps working. Launched by double-click (Explorer, Start menu, installer shortcut) there is no console and no redirect, so `camcraft_app::logging::init` writes the tracing log to a missing stderr handle and the log is lost. Only a start-up failure or panic is surfaced (message box, PR #1287).\n\nExpected: with no console and no valid stderr, the log goes to a file in a per-user location (e.g. `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\CamCraft\\logs\\camcraft-ui.log`, rotated or size-capped), and the start-up failure / panic message box names that path.\n\nNotes: a terminal launch or a redirect must keep writing where it does today. Pick the location and rotation policy in a decision note; no new dependency without the maintainer's say (tracing-appender would be one).\n\nDone means: a double-clicked `camcraft-ui.exe` on Windows writes its tracing log to a documented per-user file; the error message box names that file; terminal and redirected launches are unchanged; the pure part (path choice, \"is stderr usable\" decision) has a unit test.\n\nRefs #1278\n",
